<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113285" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χᾰμαίτῠπ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>striking its prey
				near</i> or <i>on the ground,</i> name of a certain hawk,
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετεωροθήρας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				620a31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαμαιτύπος πόρνη,</span>
			= Lat. <i>scortum,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ χαμαιτύποι</span> is
			prob. 
				f. l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ χαμαιτύπαι</span>
			 (corr. Wendland) in <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.345
			</span></i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαμαιτύπη.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
